auth {
  mode: oauth2
}

auth:oauth2 {
  grant_type: authorization_code
  callback_url: {{portalCallbackUrl}}
  authorization_url: {{centralIdp}}/auth/realms/CX-Central/protocol/openid-connect/auth
  access_token_url: {{centralIdp}}/auth/realms/CX-Central/protocol/openid-connect/token
  client_id: Cl2-CX-Portal
  client_secret:
  scope: openid
  pkce: true
}

docs {
  BE-293 diagnosis of the BPN credential failure (IssuerService NullPointerException in
  AttestationPipelineImpl.evaluate for holder BPNL00000000052O).

  Folder "Issuer (read-only)": IssuerService admin API in release26-09, x-api-key per request, GET and
  POST .../query only. Needs the tunnel:
    kubectl --kubeconfig ~/.kube/alpha.yaml --context alpha -n release26-09 port-forward svc/issuer-service 18086:8086

  Folder "Portal (operator login)": Portal administration API with the operator's own Keycloak login
  (CX-Central, public client Cl2-CX-Portal, authorization code + PKCE; Bruno opens the login window).
  The retrigger requests change the application and are guarded: they refuse to send unless confirmRetrigger
  equals applicationId. Send them only after approval and after the issuer cause is fixed.

  Secrets (issuerAdminApiKey) and tokens are kept by Bruno on this machine only, never in these files.
}
